# Conventional Commits template
# Docs: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
#
# Format:
#   <type>(optional scope)!: <subject>
#
# Types:
#   feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test,
#   build, ci, chore, revert
#
# Common scopes:
#   extension, repo, ui, sync, ai, build, deps, release, ci, docs
#
# Examples:
#   feat(extension): add typed messaging bus for content/background
#   fix(sync): reject results after a destination disconnect
#   refactor(ui): split options page into sections
#   chore(repo)!: remove deprecated shared package
#   docs: add setup instructions for a Notion token
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Include a line starting with "BREAKING CHANGE:" in the body
#   describing what changed and migration steps.
#
# Issue references:
#   Use "Closes #123" or "Refs #123" in the footer.
#
# ---------------- WRITE YOUR MESSAGE BELOW THIS LINE ----------------

# Body (why / how):
# - Explain motivation, approach, and any trade-offs

# BREAKING CHANGE: <describe breaking change and migration>

# Footer:
# Closes #
# Refs #
